# Loop C Pre-Result Design Audit — Track P First-Wave Preregs
**Mode:** packet-only, read-only, design-stage. No tools, files, network, or model calls were used. Evidence status is judged strictly from the four verbatim preregs; anything not in the packet is UNVERIFIED. Labels: FACT (stated in packet) / INFERENCE (derived from packet) / UNVERIFIED (absent from packet).

---

## PR-EXP-03
- Q1: YES (partially definitional) — INFERENCE: P1 is constructed as adjacent-column transposition while `structural_signature` includes the ordered positional header-token sequence, so `response=1` on all P1 is construction-level whenever headers move with columns; with no no-op/specificity arm a constant-1 detector also attains coverage=1, so "coverage delta > 0" is not discriminating as written.
- Q2: YES, observability only — FACT: population labels and task truth are untouched; only the instrument at `parse.table.regression` is replaced (de-aliasing), which is a measurement change, not a truth change.
- Q3: PARTIAL — FACT: UID selection rule, prior-population exclusion, and freeze order (oracle definition + implementation hash → P1 generation → evaluation, no post-observation edits) are correctly specified; UNVERIFIED: "frozen drift corpus", the prior-experiment UID exclusion registry, and the per-table pair-selection hash rule are referenced but not given verbatim in the packet.
- Q4: INCOMPLETE — FACT: both baselines (aliased v1 copy, standalone field-hit oracle) are run unchanged on the same population (good); MISSING: a no-op/identity control (must return 0) and a non-structural specificity arm, so "coverage" cannot distinguish detection quality from a constant-1 response rule.
- Q5: PARTIAL — FACT: zero model/judge calls, deterministic, GB10 minutes, freeze/audit overhead in the ledger; MISSING: a numeric cost-comparability tolerance ("same check-count budget class" is undefined) — cost inequivalence is only an INVALID trigger, not a defined gate.
- Q6: NO — UNVERIFIED: `SOURCE_LOCAL_RESPONSE` is never defined in the packet; the mandatory attribution audit has no operational test (no ablation, null channel, or counterfactual), so a source-local-only gain cannot be ruled out as written.
- Q7: PARTIAL — FACT: same-population comparison and "conclusion-level deltas only (before/after F1 never combined)" are properly declared; MISSING: the two oracles are different measurement objects and the P1 ground-truth stage/family labels underpinning the diagnosability macro-F1 are undefined.
- Q8: PARTIAL — FACT: NOT_EVALUABLE is explicitly never merged into NULL (compliant); HOLE: `coverage>0 & diagnosability<0` and `coverage=0 & diagnosability>0` are unclassified (neither POSITIVE nor NULL); "sanity gate" is referenced but undefined.
- Q9: NO — SCOPE_CHANGE: NO (repair of the filed HIGH incident at `parse.table.regression` matches owner-fixed §2; the missing items are validity controls and contract precision, not scientific-scope change).
- Q10: (1) no-op/identity control; (2) specificity / non-structural negative-control arm; (3) operational definition of the SOURCE_LOCAL_RESPONSE attribution audit; (4) P1 ground-truth stage/family labels and cluster/group unit for LOCO; (5) complete outcome taxonomy; (6) "sanity gate" definition; (7) cost-comparability tolerance; (8) verbatim hash rules for drift-corpus membership, UID exclusion registry, pair selection; (9) recorded hashes proving the v1/aliased baseline is unchanged and is the true aliased copy.
- VERDICT: CONDITIONAL
- CONDITIONS: (a) add a no-op/identity arm and a non-structural specificity arm so coverage is not attainable by a constant-1 detector, and report the FP side of the response rule; (b) operationalize the attribution audit (named ablation/null channel/counterfactual and pass criterion) or the claim must be bounded to "not evaluated for source-local attribution"; (c) complete the outcome taxonomy, including coverage-gain-with-diagnosability-loss and the reverse, and define the "sanity gate"; (d) freeze verbatim the drift-corpus membership rule, UID exclusion registry, pair-selection hash rule, and baseline implementation hashes in the implementation contract; (e) define cost tolerance and the stage/family ground-truth labeling rule for P1. All five are prereg / implementation-contract revisions; if any cannot be made without altering owner-fixed §2 scope, STOP_BRANCH for PR-EXP-03.
- SCOPE_CHANGE: NO

