## PR-EXP-04
- Q1: NO definitional gain on the endpoint (transfer is empirical) — BUT INFERENCE: the N2 visibility gate (≥2/3 injections with ≥1 response, ≥6 groups) selects on observability and is applied asymmetrically — N2 is gate-filtered while N1 rows are pre-existing frozen carriers with no stated gate — which can inflate transfer and is not a definitional guarantee but is a selection asymmetry.
- Q2: YES — FACT: stage labels and task truth are unchanged; the hypothesis concerns what the frozen instrumentation captures, and the visibility gate is an observability filter that is explicitly declared (MECHANISM_NOT_EVALUABLE), not a relabeling.
- Q3: GOOD on the stated axes — FACT: mechanism-disjoint and group-disjoint, N2 UIDs disjoint from N1 groups, generation rule frozen, double-run byte-identical, preregistered before any N2 result, extraction frozen before N2 rows observed, no feature edits after observation. UNVERIFIED: the definition of "group"; and INFERENCE: method-development history on N1 carriers can make the N2→N1 direction optimistic (the frozen codebook/features were plausibly developed on N1-like material).
- Q4: PARTIAL — FACT: chance/majority/direct-codebook control and the responsive-leaf-set overlap report are mandatory (good); MISSING: a generation-harness/provenance control (a placebo injection through the same harness, or a matched re-run of N1 rows) to separate "mechanism" from "harness artifact"; chance/majority values are referenced as frozen but not stated numerically in the packet.
- Q5: MISSING — FACT: this prereg has no cost section at all (no zero-model-call statement, no GB10 estimate, no same-budget comparison statement), unlike 03/01/07.
- Q6: HANDLED IN THE RIGHT DIRECTION — FACT: source-locality is the hypothesized failure mode here (fingerprint-bound signature), and the NULL branch is defined as collapse toward chance with the result bounding the flagship claim, plus the direct-codebook control and leaf-set overlap report; MISSING: explicit exclusion of mechanism-identifying generator artifacts from the feature surface (the extraction freeze is stated, but not a ban on provenance/harness features).
- Q7: PARTIAL — FACT: the same frozen signature, same 12-leaf surface, same frozen response rule are used in both directions, and the comparison is per-direction against frozen baselines rather than a combined before/after number; MISSING: explicit declaration that N1 and N2 rows are different populations by design (mechanism-disjoint) and that the visibility gate makes N2 conditioned-on-observability while N1 is not.
- Q8: PARTIAL — FACT: MECHANISM_NOT_EVALUABLE is explicitly never counted as a generalization failure and NULL is never merged with NOT_EVALUABLE (compliant); HOLE: a direction that falls *below* chance, a direction whose CI includes chance ("non-negative vs chance" is not numerically defined), and a direction with too few groups for a CI are all unclassified.
- Q9: NO — SCOPE_CHANGE: NO (GENERALIZATION_TEST, supporting-only, explicitly "does NOT count toward the repair count", matching the human decision; no repair credit claimed).
- Q10: (1) cost section and same-budget statement; (2) symmetric application of the visibility gate to N1 or an explicit non-comparability declaration; (3) definition of "held-out group"; (4) numerically frozen chance/majority/direct baseline values; (5) completed directional outcome taxonomy; (6) harness/provenance confound control or an explicit claim bound; (7) declaration of N1 method-development contamination of the N2→N1 direction; (8) explicit ban on provenance/mechanism-identifier features in the frozen feature surface.
- VERDICT: CONDITIONAL
- CONDITIONS: (a) add a cost section (zero-model-call statement, GB10 estimate, same-budget comparison) to the implementation contract; (b) either apply the visibility gate symmetrically to the N1 carriers or declare N1/N2 non-comparability and report gate attrition for both; (c) complete the directional taxonomy (below-chance, CI-includes-chance, insufficient-groups) with a numeric definition of "non-negative"/"strictly above"; (d) add a harness-matched control (placebo injection or re-run of N1 rows through the same generator) OR bind the conclusion explicitly to "transfer across these two mechanisms under the shared generation harness" and record the confound; (e) freeze numerically the chance/majority/direct baselines, define "group", and declare the N1-development contamination of N2→N1. All are prereg / implementation-contract revisions; supporting-only status must be preserved.
- SCOPE_CHANGE: NO

